// Two entities are compared with `==` and `!=`: the one a `for` visits,
// one a field or a unique holds, one at the other end of an arrow. They
// are the same where their ids are (`ent.same`).
// RUN: %ent run %S/Inputs/same.ent 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
// RUN: ent-translate --import-ent %S/Inputs/same.ent -I %S/../../devices \
// RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IR

// IR: ent.same

// CHECK:      a is not the chosen one
// CHECK-NEXT: b is the chosen one
// CHECK-NEXT: c is not the chosen one
// CHECK-NEXT: d is not the chosen one
// CHECK-NEXT: b likes the one it is in
// CHECK-NEXT: c likes another
// CHECK-NEXT: d likes another
